    {
      "id": 48,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        2200,
        2350
      ],
      "size": [
        640,
        230
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 48,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "widget_ue_connectable": {}
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "widgets_values": [
        "DEPTH: DepthCrafter (settings from your Depth workflow: 5 steps, window 110, overlap 25).\n\nLicence: Tencent's DepthCrafter licence is academic / research / education only (and it sits on Stable Video Diffusion, also non-commercial). Fine for testing and comparing. Check before using it on client shots.\n\nIn Nuke: if lights land on the wrong side in depth, toggle 'depth: near is white' on the Setup tab."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 50,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        4600,
        2150
      ],
      "size": [
        820,
        590
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 50,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "widget_ue_connectable": {}
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "widgets_values": [
        "INTERIM SETUP (no FLP node needed)\n\nOne ProRes file per pass is written instead of the packed file:\n  _Albedo, _Irradiance, _normal, _depth  (matte too, once un-muted)\n\nIN NUKE: Read each file with colourspace = raw, then plug into DF_comfy_relight:\n  _normal -> normals    _depth -> depth    _Albedo -> albedo    _Irradiance -> irradiance\n  _matte -> Shuffle red into alpha -> mask   (only if you want the matte; or use your own roto)\nReformat each pass up to the plate before the node, as before.\n\nMATTE: the matte saver is muted. Un-mute it (and the MaskToImage next to it) once the SAM2 click is set.\nCONTACT SHEET is muted to save time.\n\nProRes 422 keeps half the colour resolution, so normals and albedo are a touch softer than the packed 4444 file. Fine for testing the node. When FLP is installed, use the packed version instead.\n\nIf lights land on the wrong side in depth, toggle 'depth: near is white' on the Setup tab.\n\nSAM2 CLICKS: only the positive wire is connected on purpose. An empty 'negative' list makes the SAM2 node fail. If you add shift+right-click 'not this' points, connect negative_coords to coordinates_negative too."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 51,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        0,
        200
      ],
      "size": [
        860,
        400
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 51,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "widget_ue_connectable": {}
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "widgets_values": [
        "WORKING SIZE + FRAME CAP\n\nSet the size in ONE place: the resize node titled WORKING SIZE (type the same number in width and height). Everything downstream is resized from that node. Set the frame cap in the VoltLoader (frame_load_cap).\n\nNORMAL        WORKING SIZE 1280   FRAME CAP 0    (whole shot. 1920 plate -> 1280 is the everyday size)\nFINAL PUSH    WORKING SIZE 1920   FRAME CAP 0    (ABOVE the 1280 verified maximum in the note beside the resize node: expect a much longer run and more VRAM. Try it first with a short frame cap.)\nLONG SHOT, QUICK LOOK    WORKING SIZE 1280   FRAME CAP 49   (one UniVidX window; set back to 0 for the full pass)\n\nCOMPILE (UniVidX loader, 'compile_dit'): costs 60-120 s each time size or frame count changes, then runs ~20-30% faster. Leave OFF for 40-50 frame shots and quick looks; turn ON for 200+ frame runs.\n\nThe packed file is named with its size, e.g. ..._RelightPack_1280x720_00001.mov, so the 1280 and 1920 renders never overwrite each other. In Nuke swap the Read; the node is resolution independent (Reformat the passes to the plate as before). Seed is fixed so the look carries over between sizes."
      ]
    },
